{{Dialogue|Tech|Are you positive about these coordinates?|Omega|Yes. I told you. They're to a landing pad that we can use in Tipoca City.|Echo|Every platform down there will be swarming with troopers.|Omega|Not this one. Trust me.|attr=Omega tells Echo and Tech to head for the secret landing platform|src=<ref name="Return to Kamino" />}}
A '''secret landing platform''' was located outside of the main structures of [[Tipoca City]] on the [[planet]] [[Kamino]]. The platform remained hidden [[Water|underwater]] until a [[Starship|ship]] approached the coordinates that would make the platform appear. The [[Cloning|clone]] [[Omega]] had knowledge of the platform and knew it led to [[Nala Se's private lab]] in the [[city]]. Omega guided her [[squad]], [[Clone Force 99]], to the platform when they undertook a [[Rescue of Hunter|mission]] in [[19 BBY]] to save their leader, [[Hunter]], from the [[Galactic Empire]].

==Description==
{{Quote|If I go any lower, we will be in the water.''"<br />"''It's the only way to activate the platform.|Tech and Omega|<ref name="Return to Kamino" />}}
[[File:SecretLandingPlatform-RtK.png|thumb|300px|right|The secret landing platform was hidden below the ocean's surface.]]
Hidden underneath the [[ocean]] on<ref name="Return to Kamino" /> the [[Wild Space]] [[planet]]<ref name="EURWS">{{EncyclopediaCite|Exegol, the Unknown Regions and Wild Space}}</ref> [[Kamino]],<ref name="Return to Kamino" /> the secret landing platform<ref name="Platform">{{SW|url=return-to-kamino-concept-art-gallery|text="Return To Kamino" Concept Art Gallery}} {{C|Slide 6}}</ref> was circular with minimal lighting and would appear when a [[starship]] approached the [[water]]'s surface at the correct coordinates.<ref name="Return to Kamino" /> The platform was part of [[Tipoca City]],<ref name="Story Gallery" /> although it was located some distance away from the [[city]]. It connected to Kamino's [[Kamino tube system|tube system]], which allowed transit to [[Nala Se's private lab]]. From there, the main city structures could be reached. When the tunnel opened, a spherical tube vehicle would emerge and allow individuals to enter and travel through the system. The platform was detectable via scanners.<ref name="Return to Kamino" />

==History==
{{Quote|Remind me. How long were you left stranded on that Kaminoan platform before being recovered?''"<br />"''Thirty-two rotations.|Vice Admiral Rampart and Crosshair|<ref name="Solitary Clone">{{TBB|The Solitary Clone}}</ref>}}
[[File:BadBatchPlusOne-KL.png|thumb|left|350px|Clone Force 99 viewing the ruins of Tipoca City from the secret landing platform.]]
In [[19 BBY]],<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> the rogue [[clone commando]] [[squad]] [[Clone Force 99]] was directed to use the platform by their newest member, the young [[Cloning|clone]] [[Omega]], when they sought to [[Rescue of Hunter|rescue]] their leader, [[Hunter]], from the [[Galactic Empire]]. Although Omega's companions [[Tech]], [[Echo]], and [[Wrecker]] were unsure about the plan, Tech flew their [[Omicron-class attack shuttle|ship]], the [[Marauder (Omicron-class)|''Marauder'']], to the coordinates. Sure enough, the platform appeared on the [[Shuttle|ship's]] scanners, and as the platform rose out of the water, Tech landed the vessel on it. Disembarking, Omega located the entrance to the tube system and the squad traveled to the private lab used by [[Kaminoan]] [[doctor]] [[Nala Se]] via a tube vehicle. From there, the clones succeeded in infiltrating Tipoca City and rescuing Hunter.<ref name="Return to Kamino" />

The squad returned to the platform following the Empire's [[Attack on Kamino|bombardment]] of Tipoca City with their former companion [[Crosshair]],<ref name="Kamino Lost">{{TBB|Kamino Lost}}</ref> who had previously joined the Empire<ref name="Timelines" /> but escaped the [[Orbital bombardment|bombardment]] alongside his former squad. Despite the annihilation of the city, the landing platform survived the destruction. However, as [[Local day|day]] broke and the clones reached the platform, Crosshair chose not to rejoin them,<ref name="Kamino Lost" /> instead waiting on the platform while the rest of the squad left Kamino. Crosshair waited for thirty-two [[Standard day|rotations]] until an Imperial patrol discovered him. Later, when he was given a new mission by Imperial [[Vice Admiral]] [[Edmon Rampart]], the [[officer]] asked Crosshair to remind him how long he had been stranded on the platform.<ref name="Solitary Clone" />

==Behind the scenes==
The landing platform first appeared in the episode "[[Return to Kamino]]," the fifteenth episode in the [[The Bad Batch Season 1|first season]] of the animated series ''[[Star Wars: The Bad Batch]]''.<ref name="Return to Kamino" /> The episode released on [[August 6]], [[2021]].<ref name="D23">{{D23|url=everything-new-you-can-stream-on-disney-in-august-2021|text=Everything New You Can Stream on Disney+ in August 2021}}</ref> It was identified by name in the ensuing episode guide released to [[StarWars.com]] on [[August 9]] of the same year. Concept art of the secret landing platform was done by [[Lucasfilm Animation]] artist [[Jim Moore]], with one artistic rendering being dated to [[May 30]], [[2020]].<ref name="Platform" /> Moore also worked on concepts of the tube vehicles associated with the platform, with one work being dated to [[May 27]], 2020.<ref name="Vehicle">{{SW|url=return-to-kamino-concept-art-gallery|text="Return To Kamino" Concept Art Gallery}} {{C|Slide 12}}</ref>

